  body: "# DWP decision maker in the DMG\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe captured DMG calls officials acting
    on behalf of the Secretary of State decision makers, and describes evidence gathering, decisions on claims and
    administrative tasks among their functions.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nA source-specific institutional role.
    This project, its AI tools and a website user do not acquire decision-making authority. Training, authorisation
    and separation of duties require operational review.\n\n## Inspected source passages\n\n- [DMG 01001, PDF page
    2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=2) — DMG Vol
    1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n- [DMG 01004, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68e8e657cf65bd04bad76752/dmg-v-1-ch-01.pdf#page=2)
    — DMG Vol 1 Ch 1: Principles of decision making and evidence.\n\n## Evidence and review status\n\nModel-assisted
    interpretation of the 15 September 2026 source snapshot; unreviewed and requiring specialist review. The source
    is DWP guidance, not a consolidated statement of legislation. This is an independent experimental publication,
    not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule.\n\nPDF page numbers are
    one-based file positions. Machine extraction can alter reading order, footnotes and characters. Quoted relationships
    preserve extracted text; no visual or specialist acceptance is claimed. Source dates, legal effects and current
    applicability remain separate review tasks.\n\n- `dmg-vol1-ch1` PDF SHA-256: `58b168c7b0a01f54713f6cfa60953549ebc099cbe568ffaeea551d0b756495d2`;
    extracted pages SHA-256: `cf7a000e2c54c5361a03ec4ad73fa22cc14e8cdb0d4f03b53919a4a509a6eacb`.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/dmg-evidence-assessment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source includes gathering information among decision-maker functions; the relation does not
      confer official authority on the project.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol1-ch1/0002
      quote: "01004 The DM takes all necessary actions on behalf of the Secretary of State, including\n\n\n1. gathering
        information\n\n\n2. making decisions on claims and applications\n\n\n3. dealing with administrative matters
        such as suspension of payment.\n\n\nNote: The DM is not an independent officer."
      locator: DMG 01004
